-- DUMPFLUX producer whose SUMMARY section asks for FLUXALL and nothing else.
--
-- A sector cut out of this model still has to evaluate the deck's UDQ and
-- ACTIONX expressions, but it no longer computes what they refer to: the
-- wells, groups and regions they name may lie outside the sector. Those
-- values have to be carried over from this run, so this run has to have
-- reported them.
--
-- Working out which vectors those are by hand means reading every UDQ and
-- every ACTIONX condition in the deck and then naming the objects each one
-- could match. FLUXALL is how the deck says "report whatever my own
-- expressions will ask for" instead.
RUNSPEC

WATER
GAS
OIL

METRIC

UNIFOUT

DIMENS
  10 1 10 /

TABDIMS
  1 1 40 20 1 20 /

WELLDIMS
  2 10 2 2 /

UDQDIMS
  10 2 0 10 10 10 0 10 /

UDADIMS
  10 0 10 /

REGDIMS
  3 1 0 0 /

ACTDIMS
  4 20 10 10 /

GRID

DX
  100*1 /
DY
  100*1 /
DZ
  100*1 /

TOPS
  10*0. /

PORO
  100*0.3 /

PERMX
  100*500 /

PERMY
  100*500 /

PERMZ
  100*500 /

-- Two cells are inactive, so a cell's index among the active ones differs
-- from its global one for everything after them. Restart arrays are written
-- per active cell while a region is described in global indices, so anything
-- that confuses the two reads the wrong cell here. Neither cell borders any
-- of the sectors the tests select, so the boundaries themselves are unchanged.
ACTNUM
  8*1 2*0 90*1 /

FLUXNUM
  10*0 1 89*0 /

FLUXTYPE
  PRESSURE /

DUMPFLUX /

INIT

PROPS

PVTW
  4017.55 1.038 3.22E-6 0.318 0.0 /

ROCK
  14.7 3E-6 /

SWOF
0.12 0 1 0
0.18 4.64876033057851E-008 1 0
0.24 0.000000186 0.997 0
