/

REGIONS

FIPNUM
  50*1
  50*2 /

SOLUTION

SWAT
  100*0.0 /

SGAS
  100*0.0 /

PRESSURE
  100*300.0 /

SUMMARY

-- The point of the case: not one vector is named here. FLUXALL is expected to
-- work out that the UDQs want WBHP, that the ACTIONX wants GEFF and RPR, and
-- that both user defined quantities have to be reported in their own right,
-- and to cover every well, group and region there is.
FLUXALL

SCHEDULE

WELSPECS
  'P1' 'G1' 3 1 1* 'OIL' /
  'P2' 'G1' 8 1 1* 'OIL' /
/

COMPDAT
  'P1' 3 1 1 10 'OPEN' 1* 1* 0.2 /
  'P2' 8 1 1 10 'OPEN' 1* 1* 0.2 /
/

WCONPROD
  'P1' 'OPEN' 'ORAT' 0.1 4* 250.0 /
  'P2' 'OPEN' 'ORAT' 0.1 4* 250.0 /
/

-- WUTWICE refers to WBHP, a well keyword. WUFOUR refers to WUTWICE, which is
-- not a summary keyword at all but another user defined quantity, and
-- UDQDefine::required_summary() drops it for that reason.
--
-- WUFOUR is also left without a UNITS entry on purpose. That is no reason to
-- withhold the vector: the summary writer emits an empty unit string for a
-- UDQ that has none, the same as it would if the deck had named WUFOUR in its
-- SUMMARY section outright.
UDQ
  DEFINE WUTWICE WBHP * 2 /
  UNITS  WUTWICE BARSA /
  DEFINE WUFOUR WUTWICE * 2 /
/

-- Refers to GEFF, a group keyword, to RPR, a region one, and to WUFOUR, which
-- reaches the rest of the chain.
ACTIONX
  ACT1  10  1 /
  GEFF  'G1'   > 0.5 AND /
  RPR   1      > 1.0 AND /
  WUFOUR 'P1'  > 0.0 /
/

WELOPEN
  'P2' 'OPEN' /
/

ENDACTIO

TSTEP
  1 /

END
